  "decision": "The sole complete hunk removes the unused Rule named import from the modern private M3 Sass test, retaining parse and every compile/assertion statement. The complete original file has no Rule identifier beyond that import. The installed diagnostic TypeScript emits identical before/after programs under the recorded options; this does not qualify every supported compiler. The add-on does not import that private upstream spec, and its library compilation excludes specs. No Sass implementation is changed by the patch. The independent Material16 M2 model, all651 exports, all498 arguments and mixed M2/M3 consumer checks remain separate requirements.",
